## Constraints

- Do NOT re-score the dimensions. The gorilla-4dim template already produced the scores. You are evaluating whether the scores are defensible.
- The floor/ceiling values are fixed by this registry. Do not propose alternative thresholds.
- A maturity block on Choke Point (because Combinatorial Solution < 50) means the Choke Point score is not credible — the lisp.eval scoring step should treat it as nil, not as the elicited value.
- A ceiling violation on Invisible Gorilla (>90) is an overconfidence signal — the analyst may be the one with the blind spot. Flag it, do not silently discount.
- Do not fabricate evidence. If a dimension has no signal in the Company Board, the gorilla-4dim template already scored it < 50; your floor check confirms the deprivation.
